				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khym-chanur" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(163438); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=163438&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607331386" alt="Khym Chanur" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=163438)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/khym-chanur" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(163438); return false;" >Khym Chanur</a></span> <span class="odate time_1341281019 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jul 2012 02:03</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1497131">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Homes found to be infected with SCP-1684 are to be occupied by task force members.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So MTF members are to act as permanent squatters, without the neighbors ever noticing and calling the police? It would probably be better to either have the property condemned or seized through imminent domain, to prevent anyone from buying it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Foundation agents who have followed up on the advertised addresses have only found abandoned buildings, and phone numbers have led to inactive numbers.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think you should make it a bit clearer that it's the Hearth Home Realty offices which appear abandoned.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After this disappearance, a sign advertising for Hearth Home Realty will appear at both the previously affected house and the house previously occupied by the disappeared persons.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, X is living at 123 Main Street, Anytown USA. X sells the house to Y, buys an instance of SCP-1684 and moves into it. After X disappears and 123 Main Street becomes a new SCP instance, what happens to Y? Does he and his furniture disappear too? Does Y end up at the warehouses as well?</p>
<p>Also, what about the neighbors. Do they not notice that their neighbors keep disappearing?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These warehouses were found to be filled with furniture and other consumer goods believed to have originated from homes affected by SCP-1684. In addition, approximately 600 people who had previously disappeared due to SCP-1684's effect were located. When questioned, they reported that they believed they were still living in their home, and described their life and current circumstance as ideal.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What about the people who were observing the house when the occupants disappear? If they're present at the warehouse, do they think they're living at a non-existent house that they bought from Hearth Home Realty, or do they somehow integrate into the household that disappeared?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Affected persons did not respond to amnesiacs and were sent to mental institutions with forged identification documents.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since the warehouses and their inhabitants escaped the notice of the locals before being found by the Foundation, why not let them continue living there while posting a guard around the warehouses? If they're sent to mental institutions they might contact relatives, and claims of being forced into a mental institution by a shadowy organization could be picked up on by various Groups of Interest.</p>

							</div>

								
					
