					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1204404&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607331386" alt="wishun" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1204404)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wishun" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1204404); return false;" >wishun</a></span> <span class="odate time_1341337253 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jul 2012 17:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1497797">
									

<p>I want to like it, but I don't; and it's very frustrating that I can't pin down why I don't.</p>
<p>The basic idea is solid, an anomalous <em>and</em> crooked realty company. I like that the people and their stuff are found, vanishing-without-a-trace is an SCP trope and I like to see something different. Victims being immune to amnesiacs doesn't add much, but it another departure from standard. Every detail I focus on seems good, but as a whole I'm left with a generally negative reaction and nothing to blame it on. Very annoying.</p>
<p>No vote until I can figure out what my heads doing and have something constructive to say (don't hold your breath).</p>

